.SH Unified architecture
All six bindings follow the same layered architecture:
.IP
.EX
  errors  \-\->  types  \-\->  protocol  \-\->  transport  \-\->  channels  \-\->  client
.EE
.PP
\f[B]errors\f[R] \(en Exception/error type hierarchy.
Five error categories map to the same failure modes across all
languages: authentication failure, protocol violation, operation
timeout, transport I/O error, and server\-returned error.
.PP
\f[B]types\f[R] \(en Data structures for channel messages.
Each language uses its native type system (dataclasses, interfaces,
structs, POJOs) to represent \f[CR]EvalResult\f[R], \f[CR]VarInfo\f[R],
\f[CR]Breakpoint\f[R], \f[CR]PreCommandEvent\f[R], and other protocol
objects.
.PP
\f[B]protocol\f[R] \(en NDJSON frame encoding and decoding.
Serializes language\-native objects to JSON\-line strings and
deserializes incoming lines back to native objects.
Handles base64 encoding for binary payloads.
.PP
\f[B]transport\f[R] \(en Connection management.
Four transport modes are supported: Unix domain socket, stdio
(subprocess), file descriptor, and Windows Named Pipe.
Each transport provides a line\-oriented read/write interface.
.PP
\f[B]channels\f[R] \(en Channel\-specific logic.
Six channel classes (one per v2 channel) encapsulate the
request/response patterns and server\-push dispatch for their respective
channel.
.PP
\f[B]client\f[R] \(en Top\-level entry point.
The \f[CR]BashClient\f[R] class ties everything together: it owns the
transport, starts a background reader, routes incoming messages to
channel queues, and exposes convenience methods for common operations.
.SH Common API lifecycle
Every client binding follows the same lifecycle:
.IP
.EX
connect  \-\->  auth  \-\->  use channels  \-\->  close
.EE
.IP "1." 3
\f[B]Connect\f[R] \(en Establish a transport connection.
The client provides factory methods for each transport mode:
\f[CR]connect()\f[R] for Unix socket, \f[CR]connect_stdio()\f[R] for
subprocess, \f[CR]connect_fd()\f[R] for inherited file descriptor, and
\f[CR]connect_named_pipe()\f[R] for Windows Named Pipes.
.IP "2." 3
\f[B]Authenticate\f[R] \(en Send an \f[CR]auth\f[R] message on
CHAN_CONTROL with the server token.
The server responds with \f[CR]auth_ok\f[R] or \f[CR]auth_fail\f[R].
All channels except CHAN_CONTROL require authentication.
.IP "3." 3
\f[B]Use channels\f[R] \(en Interact with the six v2 channels through
the channel objects exposed on the client (\f[CR]control\f[R],
\f[CR]command\f[R], \f[CR]state\f[R], \f[CR]observe\f[R],
\f[CR]debug\f[R], \f[CR]pty\f[R]).
Each channel provides methods for its message types.
.IP "4." 3
\f[B]Close\f[R] \(en Send a \f[CR]disconnect\f[R] message, cancel the
background reader, and close the transport.
.SH Quick comparison
\f[B]Python\f[R] (async/await):
.IP
.EX
\f[B]async\f[R] \f[B]with\f[R] BashClient.connect(\(dq/tmp/bash\-server\-1000/sock\(dq) \f[B]as\f[R] client:
    \f[B]await\f[R] client.auth(token)
    result = \f[B]await\f[R] client.eval(\(dqecho hello\(dq)
    print(result.stdout)
.EE
.PP
\f[B]TypeScript\f[R] (Promise\-based):
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] client = \f[B]await\f[R] BashClient.connect(\(dq/tmp/bash\-server\-1000/sock\(dq);
\f[B]try\f[R] {
    \f[B]await\f[R] client.auth(token);
    \f[B]const\f[R] result = \f[B]await\f[R] client.eval(\(dqecho hello\(dq);
    console.log(result.stdout);
} \f[B]finally\f[R] {
    \f[B]await\f[R] client.close();
}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]C\f[R] (synchronous blocking):
.IP
.EX
bc_client_t *c = bc_connect(\(dq/tmp/bash\-server\-1000/sock\(dq);
bc_auth(c, token);
bc_eval_result_t result;
bc_eval(c, \(dqecho hello\(dq, &result);
printf(\(dq%s\(dq, result.stdout_data);
bc_eval_result_free(&result);
bc_close(c);
.EE
.PP
\f[B]Java\f[R] (blocking with try\-with\-resources):
.IP
.EX
\f[B]try\f[R] (BashClient client = BashClient.connect(\(dq/tmp/bash\-server\-1000/sock\(dq)) {
    client.auth(token);
    EvalResult result = client.eval(\(dqecho hello\(dq);
    System.out.println(result.stdout);
}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]Go\f[R] (goroutine\-based with context):
.IP
.EX
client, err := bashclient.Connect(ctx, \(dq/tmp/bash\-server\-1000/sock\(dq)
\f[B]if\f[R] err != nil { log.Fatal(err) }
\f[B]defer\f[R] client.Close()
client.Auth(ctx, token)
result, _ := client.Eval(ctx, \(dqecho hello\(dq)
fmt.Print(result.Stdout)
.EE
.PP
\f[B]C#\f[R] (Task\-based async/await):
.IP
.EX
await \f[B]using\f[R] var client = await BashClient.ConnectAsync(\(dq/tmp/bash\-server\-1000/sock\(dq);
await client.AuthAsync(token);
var result = await client.EvalAsync(\(dqecho hello\(dq);
Console.Write(result.Stdout);
.EE
