.PP
The Python and TypeScript bindings use exception inheritance trees
rooted at \f[CR]BashClientError\f[R].
The C binding uses integer return codes (\f[CR]BC_OK\f[R],
\f[CR]BC_ERR_*\f[R]).
The Java binding uses checked exceptions as static inner classes of
\f[CR]BashClientException\f[R].
The Go binding uses concrete error types implementing the
\f[CR]error\f[R] interface, checked via \f[CR]errors.As()\f[R].
The C# binding uses an exception hierarchy rooted at
\f[CR]BashClientException\f[R].
